# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — hot-reload pattern.
#
# The live-code-update pattern the service exists for: define a
# function, call it, redefine it on a later line, call it again and get
# the NEW body.  Both lines run against the same session realm, which is
# what makes the second definition replace the first rather than land in
# a fresh world.
#
# Named-function declarations are not a v1.0 form; `var name =
# function(...) { ... }` is, per the lexer's diagnostic.

# Define f returning 1.

## mode: repl
> {"id":7,"op":"eval","code":"var f = function() { 1 } | f()"}
< "id":7 | "kind":"result" | "value":"1"
< "id":7 | "kind":"done"

# Redefine f returning 2.
> {"id":8,"op":"eval","code":"var f = function() { 2 } | f()"}
< "id":8 | "kind":"result" | "value":"2"
< "id":8 | "kind":"done"
